#, no-wrap
msgid "Army rules"
msgstr "Règles de l'Armée"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "The things in the woods"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:93
msgid ""
"Beastmen infantry do not suffer the usual −1 Command penalty when within "
"woodland."
msgstr ""

#. 3: its
#. 5: if not → unless, roll, its
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[gor-ungor,†1]]1. Gor/Ungor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:107
msgid ""
"Up to half the Gor units (rounded down) and half the Ungor units (rounded "
"down) may be designated as Ambushers. At the start of the game, you must "
"inform your opponent how many units will Ambush. Ambushers may form Brigades "
"or act as single units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:115
msgid ""
"Ambushers are deployed during any Command phase, not at the start of the "
"game. To deploy ambushers, nominate a character, the ambushing units and a "
"point in a piece of dense terrain or a point on any board edge except the "
"enemy’s.  Issue an Ambush order to the point, which can be outside the "
"character’s Command range. Apply distance and enemy proximity penalties, but "
"ignore dense terrain penalties."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:123
msgid ""
"If the Ambush order is successful, place one stand from the unit at the "
"point, then deploy the rest in formation around it.  Brigade units form up "
"within a full pace move of the first stand.  If the nominated point is in "
"dense terrain it must be chosen that every stand of every unit within the "
"group must be at least partially within the terrain. No Ambusher may deploy "
"within 1cm of an enemy stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:128
msgid ""
"After deployment, Ambushers may receive further orders if in the Command "
"range, but the Ambush order counts as their first order. If the Ambush order "
"fails, Ambushers cannot deploy that turn but can try again later in the game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:130
msgid "Once deployed, Ambushers operate like normal units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:132
msgid "Ungor have a shooting range of 15 cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:133
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[minotaurs,†2]]2. Minotaurs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:137
msgid ""
"Minotaurs are subject for Bloodlust – they always use initiative to charge "
"if possible and cannot be given orders instead. A unit with Bloodlust never "
"use initiative to evade and must pursue or advance where possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:141
msgid ""
"Also, it is immune to terror, cannot be driven back by shooting and never "
"rolls for drive backs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[centigors,†3]]3. Centigors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:147
msgid ""
"Centigors have a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in "
"this unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading "
"and shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit "
"still needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Les Centigors ont une portée de tir de 15cm et une vision à 360° - c'est-à-"
"dire que les socles de l'unité peuvent tracer une ligne de vue depuis "
"n'importe quel bord de leur socle, ceci afin d'éviter ou de tirer, incluant "
"le tir sur les ennemis en charge. Notez que l'unité a tout de même besoin "
"d'avoir une Ligne de Vue depuis son bord avant pour charger un ennemi."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:148
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dragon-ogres,†4]]4. Dragon Ogres"
msgstr "[[dragon-ogres,†4]]4. Dragons Ogres"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:149
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:128
msgid "Dragon Ogres are immune to terror."
msgstr "Les Dragons Ogres sont immunisés à la terreur."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[chaos-spawn,†5]]5. Chaos Spawn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Spawn units have −1 Command penalty unless part of a brigade that includes "
"more non-Spawn units than Spawn units. Up to two Spawn units can be included "
"in any brigade and do not count towards the maximum size of that brigade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:161
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:139
msgid ""
"Spawn units cause terror in combat – enemies suffer the −1 Combat modifier "
"for fighting terrifying creatures. Spawn units cannot be driven back by "
"shooting and never roll for drive backs. Spawn units must pursue or advance "
"if victorious in combat where it is permitted to do so."
msgstr ""
"Les Enfants du Chaos causent la terreur, et l’ennemi subit donc un malus de "
"-1 Attaque pour combattre ces ennemis terrifiants. Les Enfants du Chaos ne "
"peuvent être repoussés au tir et ne lancent jamais de jet de repoussement. "
"Les Enfants du Chaos doivent poursuivre ou avancer s'ils sont victorieux "
"lors d'un combat, quand cela leur est permis."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:167
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:145
msgid ""
"Spawn units have a shooting range of 15cm and 360° vision – the unit can "
"draw line of sight from all edges of its stand for the purpose of evading "
"and shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit "
"still needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Les Enfants du Chaos ont une portée de tir de 15cm et une vision à 360° - "
"c'est-à-dire que les socles de l'unité peuvent tracer une ligne de vue "
"depuis n'importe quel bord de leur socle, ceci afin d'éviter ou de tirer, "
"incluant le tir sur les ennemis en charge. Notez que l'unité a tout de même "
"besoin d'avoir une Ligne de Vue depuis son bord avant pour charger un ennemi."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:168
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dragon-ogre-shaggoth,†6]]6. Dragon Ogre Shaggoth"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:171
msgid ""
"Dragon Ogre Shaggoth must always be given a separate order. It cannot be "
"brigaded with other troops even with other Shaggoths."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:183
msgid ""
"Shaggoth has a great many hits, 8 in fact, which are almost impossible to "
"inflict during even a fairly lengthy combat engagement. Because Shaggoths "
"have so many hits we must consider the possibility of hurting the Dragon "
"Ogre Shaggoth and reducing its effectiveness in subsequent turns. Therefore, "
"if a Shaggoth has accumulated 5–7 hits by the end of the Shooting phase or "
"Combat phase and is no longer engaged in combat it is deemed to have been "
"badly hurt. Once a Shaggoth is badly hurt then all accumulated hits are "
"discounted and its maximum Hits value and Attacks are halved for the rest of "
"the battle (to 4 Hits and 4 Attacks)."
msgstr ""
"Un Shaggoth possède beaucoup de Points de Vie (8). Il serait donc très "
"difficile d’en venir à bout même lors d'un même combat. À cause de cela, "
"nous devons considérer la possibilité que les blessures subies réduisent son "
"efficacité au combat. De ce fait, si un Shaggoth a accumulé entre 5 et 7 "
"touches à la fin d’une phase de Tir ou de Combat, et qu'il n'est plus "
"engagé, il est grièvement blessé. Une fois qu’un Shaggoth est grièvement "
"blessé, toutes les touches accumulées jusque-là sont annulées mais ses "
"Attaques et ses Points de Vie sont réduits de moitié pour le reste de la "
"partie (4 Attaques et 4 Points de Vie)."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:186
msgid "A Dragon Ogre Shaggoth causes terror in its enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[doombull,†7]]7. Doombull"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:191
msgid ""
"A unit joined by a Doombull cause terror. Also, Gors, Ungors and Bestigors "
"joined by a Doombull will become subject to Bloodlust in the same way as "
"Minotaur units, until the end of the following Beastmen Command phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:192
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[tuskgor-chariot,†8]]8. Tuskgor Chariot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:194
msgid ""
"Beastlord or Wargors can ride a Tuskgor Chariot. A character riding a "
"chariot adds +1 to his Attacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beastmen spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "Traitor Kin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:207
msgid ""
"_The Shaman dominates the beasts used by the enemy, turning them on their "
"masters._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:214
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any enemy unit of Cavalry, Chariots or Monsters "
"within range regardless of whether the Shaman can see it or not. The spell "
"takes effect until the end of the opposing player’s next turn. Whilst the "
"spell lasts the unit cannot use its Initiative. Any order given to the unit, "
"or to any brigade of which the unit is a part, suffers a −1 Command penalty."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:216
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hunting for Gore!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:224
msgid ""
"_The Shaman’s magic power arouses in the herd an uncontrollable desire to "
"tear asunder any enemy and feast on their bloody remains. Rows of wild "
"warriors charge headlong into their foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:231
msgid ""
"The spell can be cast on unengaged friendly unit within range regardless of "
"whether the Shaman can see it or not. The spell affects only a single unit, "
"never a brigade. The unit can be moved just as if it had received an order "
"in the Command phase.  Character stands that have joined the unit will not "
"move with it – they remain where they are."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chaos Bolt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:240
msgid ""
"_The dark power of Chaos pulses through the Shaman. A foul incantation flows "
"from his mouth which calls down a mighty lightning bolt from the heavens "
"above that strikes the enemy._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:247
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on an enemy unit. The Shaman must be able to see his "
"target to use this spell. The spell cannot be directed at a unit engaged in "
"combat. The Chaos Bolt is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks "
"except that armour has no effect (all targets count as having no armour). A "
"unit can be driven back by a Chaos Bolt as with ordinary shooting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Power of Herd"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:256
msgid ""
"_The Beastman Herd rise on the Shaman’s command.  Emboldened by his fervour "
"they charge at the enemy with unbridled fury._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:263
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on all Gor, Ungor and Centigor units engaged in close "
"combat and within range regardless of whether the Shaman can see them or "
"not. When the spell is successfully cast, each affected unit receives "
"additional +1 Attack per stand (including character stands) for the duration "
"of its first following combat engagement. Additional Attack bonus does not "
"apply when these units advance into next enemies."
msgstr ""
